  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme for Country Partnership for Senegal (2026#2030)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The second phase of the UNIDO Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) in Senegal is conceived as a catalyst for the country#s transformation into a diversified, resilient, and inclusive industrial economy. Building on the solid foundation established during the first phase (2015#2024), this new phase is intricately aligned with Senegal#s landmark #Senegal 2050: National Agenda for Transformation,# the government#s five-year action plan for 2025#2029, and key sectoral strategies such as the #Lettre de Politique d#Industrialisation.# The overarching aim is to accelerate structural economic transformation, foster regional balance, and nurture national industrial champions, all while ensuring that industrialization remains inclusive and sustainable.  At the heart of PCP Senegal Phase II is a commitment to deepen the impact of ongoing initiatives while introducing innovative projects that respond to the evolving needs of the country#s industrial sector. The programme#s design reflects extensive consultations with government ministries, national agencies, the private sector, and development partners, ensuring that interventions are both relevant and responsive to national priorities and bottlenecks. The programme#s strategic focus is on supporting Senegal#s eight territorial poles-Dakar, Thi&#xe8;s, Centre, South, South-E</narrative>
  </description>
